+# 01: Import new contacts from a well-formed file (tracer bullet)
+
+**What to build:** Sales can hand contactbook a CSV file with the export's columns, and every row becomes a new contact. The import report lists the created contacts. This is the thinnest end-to-end path through the import interface described in the spec (`.scratch/csv-import/spec.md`). Later tickets build on it.
+
+**Blocked by:** None (can start immediately)
+
+**Status:** resolved
+
+- [ ] `import_contacts(repo, data)`, `ImportReport` and `RowIssue` exist with exactly the interface in the spec.
+- [ ] `ImportFileError` exists as a ContactError subclass and is exported from the package alongside the other domain errors.
+- [ ] `data` may be decoded text or UTF-8 bytes. A leading byte-order mark is accepted in both.
+- [ ] Header columns are matched ignoring case and surrounding spaces, in any order. `name` and `email` are required; `phone` and `tags` are optional.
+- [ ] Each row creates a contact with values normalised exactly as when contacts are added by hand. An empty phone cell means no phone.
+- [ ] The tags cell is split on `;`, with each piece trimmed and empty pieces dropped.
+- [ ] `created` lists the normalised emails in file order.
+- [ ] A file with only a header returns an empty report.
+- [ ] File errors (raise `ImportFileError`, repository unchanged): an empty file; no header, including a blank first line; no email column; no name column.
+- [ ] Round trip: CSV produced by the existing export imports into an empty repository and recreates the same contacts.
+
+## Comments
+
