+# 04: Duplicate emails within one file
+
+**What to build:** When the same email appears on more than one row of a file, the first row claims it. Every later row with that email is a row error pointing back at the first row. Sales sees the conflict instead of one version silently winning.
+
+**Blocked by:** 02 (Row errors, phone warnings and row numbering)
+
+**Status:** resolved
+
+- [ ] Emails are compared after normalisation, so differences in case or surrounding spaces still count as the same email.
+- [ ] A later row with an email used by an earlier row is a row error with `column="email"`. Its message names the earlier row (e.g. "same email as row 3"), and the row is not applied.
+- [ ] The first row with an email claims it even if that row itself has a row error. Later rows with that email are still duplicates.
+- [ ] A row whose email can't be normalised claims nothing.
+- [ ] An email appears in `created` or `updated` at most once, and never in both.
+
