+# 05: Clear file errors for wrongly saved files
+
+**What to build:** When Sales saves the spreadsheet in a way contactbook can't read, the whole file is rejected with a file error. The message says how to fix it, and nothing is imported. Columns contactbook doesn't know are ignored with a warning instead of blocking the import.
+
+**Blocked by:** 01 (Import new contacts from a well-formed file)
+
+**Status:** resolved
+
+- [ ] Bytes that are not valid UTF-8 raise `ImportFileError`, with a message telling the user to save as "CSV UTF-8". There is no fallback encoding.
+- [ ] A semicolon-separated file raises `ImportFileError`, with a message telling the user to export as comma-separated. The trigger is a header that, read as comma-separated, is a single cell containing `;`.
+- [ ] A malformed CSV, such as a quote that is never closed, raises `ImportFileError`.
+- [ ] A column named twice in the header (after ignoring case and spaces) raises `ImportFileError`.
+- [ ] An unknown column is ignored and produces one warning with `row=1`, `column` = the header text as written, and a message saying it was ignored.
+- [ ] In every `ImportFileError` case the repository is unchanged.
+
