+# Contactbook
+
+The core of the contacts service: the people we keep in touch with and the ways contacts get in and out of the book.
+
+## Language
+
+**Contact**:
+A person we keep in touch with, identified by their email address.
+_Avoid_: Lead, person, entry
+
+### Import
+
+**Import**:
+Loading a whole CSV file of contacts into the book in one go. The file has the same columns as the export.
+_Avoid_: Upload, bulk add
+
+**Row**:
+One line of an import file, numbered the way the spreadsheet shows it: the header is row 1 and every line counts, blank ones included.
+_Avoid_: Line, record, entry
+
+**Blank row**:
+A row with no content at all, or only empty or whitespace cells. It is skipped without comment.
+
+**Created contact**:
+A contact that the import added because no contact had its email yet.
+
+**Updated contact**:
+An existing contact that an import row changed.
+
+**Row error**:
+A problem that kept one row from being imported. The other rows are still imported.
+_Avoid_: Failure, rejection
+
+**Row warning**:
+Something in a row worth a look that does not by itself keep the row from being imported, such as an unusable phone number.
+
+**File error**:
+A problem with the file as a whole that stops the import entirely, so nothing is imported.
+_Avoid_: Fatal error
+
+**Import report**:
+The account of an import: which contacts were created and updated, plus the row errors and row warnings.
